  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607195200: Collision-free nested and branch-local Wasm allocation

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

The primary Kotoba Wasm emitter treats every function's locals as one index
namespace. Internal locals emitted while compiling a let binding RHS are
reserved before assigning the binding. Internal locals emitted by an if test
are reserved before compiling the then branch, and then-branch locals are
reserved before compiling the else branch. This prevents both later-expression
reuse and mixed i32/i64 branch collisions.

The PostgreSQL session component is retained as the motivating executable
case: its boolean SSL negotiation test and i64 TLS handle previously collided.
The existing pair linear-memory regression additionally proves that reserving
temporary slots does not alias later pair bindings.

## Maturity boundary

This closes the observed local-index collision class for the primary emitter.
It is not a formal verifier proof and does not replace Wasm engine validation;
every emitted production artifact must still pass the engine validator."}]
